From 60d1b7c892b8dedd88826be065c82f8935c37ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:37:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add update --resources: change a container's rctl limits in
 place

CRI-O implements the CRI UpdateContainerResources call (Kubernetes in-place
pod resize) by running '<runtime> update --resources - <id>' with OCI
linux.resources on stdin, as runc does; ocijail had no update command.

The update is merged into the container's stored linux.resources (fields
absent or null keep their value, as with runc), translated with
rctl::from_oci_resources, and the jail's managed rules are replaced: rctl
keeps rules with the same subject, resource and action side by side and
the lowest wins, so each managed resource:action is removed before the new
rule is added. Like Linux refusing a memory.max below usage (EBUSY), a
memory limit below the jail's current memoryuse is refused rather than
letting memoryuse:sigkill kill the container (best effort: racctd samples
memoryuse once per second).

Tests: merge_oci_resources unit tests; test_update_resources (memory-only
and cpu-only updates, persistence, refusal below usage, stopped container).
